Severnye Obyekty: 42 million ₽ per year, 14% of company revenue, client for three years, renewal in ten weeks.

Account manager's notes from the last two meetings:
— the request comes from the COO, not the economic buyer. The CFO pays, and they haven't mentioned this;
— the client underwent an audit that flagged 'insufficient approval controls' in several systems, including ours;
— when asked what exactly the audit requires, the COO replied: 'So that expensive requests don't go to work without a manager's signature, and this is visible in the log';
— he describes their approval hierarchy as 'five levels, but only two actually work'.
